\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces An outline of the suggested framework for cross-modal knowledge transfer. Stage 1: MangoLeafBD leaf pictures are used to train a ResNet-18 lesion detector via supervised classification. Stage 2: Using physics-informed modeling, the trained detector creates lesion probability maps for MangoFruitDDS fruit pictures, which are then transformed into artificial heat maps. Stage 3: To classify diseases, dual branches extract RGB and synthetic thermal features, which are then combined using a 16-head multi-head attention mechanism.}}{5}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:architecture_final}{{1}{5}{An outline of the suggested framework for cross-modal knowledge transfer. Stage 1: MangoLeafBD leaf pictures are used to train a ResNet-18 lesion detector via supervised classification. Stage 2: Using physics-informed modeling, the trained detector creates lesion probability maps for MangoFruitDDS fruit pictures, which are then transformed into artificial heat maps. Stage 3: To classify diseases, dual branches extract RGB and synthetic thermal features, which are then combined using a 16-head multi-head attention mechanism}{figure.caption.1}{}}
